  from a shutdown if democrats and  republicans can't agree on a path  forward to fund our government right now  the two sides sparring over a democratic  push to attach a debt ceiling height to  that 3.5 trillion dollar spending plan  republicans are refusing to support that  effort  if they want to tax borrow and spend  historic sums of money without our input  they'll have to raise the debt limit  without our help i didn't want to vote  for it when trump was president but i  did because my obligation is to pay our  bills so that we can make veterans va  benefit payments so we can make social  security payment now the house already  passed a bill to fund the government and  raise the debt ceiling but democrats  need at least 10 republicans to pass the  plan over in the senate unless they  managed to use what is called budget  reconciliation  john langler talked with our washington  d.c correspondent alexandra limon to  explain exactly what that means  democrats are hoping to pass that 3.5  trillion dollar spending plan using  budget reconciliation it's a term we've  heard a lot about lately but  it's pretty technical alex simone  joining us from washington to to talk  about it and what this budget  reconciliation what it really is alex  hey there well budget reconciliation is  a process by which lawmakers try to pass  a budget to put it simply now in the u.s  house lawmakers always only need a  simple majority in order to pass a piece  of legislation but that is not the case  in the senate because of the filibuster  senators need to have 60 senators  support  a piece of legislation in order to pass  it the budget reconciliation however  provides an exemption to that rule any  bill that or any package that is passed  under this process of budget  reconciliation can be passed with only a  simple majority and that is why both  parties really try to use that process  when they can to try to pass major  pieces of legislation republicans for  example use that process to pass their  tax cuts which also provided you know  big tax cuts to corporations they  slashed the corporate tax rate and now  democrats are trying to do the same  thing trying to approve their spending  plan plan 3.5 trillion dollars that  would invest in things like free  preschool community college and also  make big investments in green energy to  try to fight climate change they too are  trying to pass it under budget  reconciliation which again would only  require a simple majority in the senate  so alex again as you said it's a  technical uh situation there in capitol  hill is a technical process only  requires that simple majority the  democrats there's a big push to get it  done but they still haven't gotten it  done where do things stand right now  with getting this all approved and  pushing it through  yeah although democrats have the  majority in the senate they've still not  been able to reach an agreement within  their own party in order to actually get  that done and get that budget  reconciliation package passed and that's  because there's some disagreement some  pretty big disagreement between the more  progressive members of the caucus and  then the more moderate members of the  caucus like joe manchin and kristin  cinema for example who don't agree with  various different things the large price  tag of it for example 3.5 3.5 trillion  dollars but also some of the other  measures uh west virginia obviously  being a big coal country area so joe  manchin perhaps pushing back on some of  those green energy initiatives and what  that would do for the coal industry in  his state  so we're seeing a lot of disagreement  and so far democrats have just had  trouble getting all of the members of  their own party in the senate to agree  and that was alex limon from washington  day marking four years since 1 october  in what to watch tonight there will be a  remembrance over at the healing garden  we will be covering that on 1 october  all day long here at channel 8. and as  alex just mentioned the budget runs out  tuesday we are waiting to see some kind  of continuing resolution if that passes  or  if we will have yet another government  shutdown next week thanks for watching  politics now you can stay up to date  online anytime and watch us here every  saturday night have a great night

